Subject: AOT: the generator API exports the short plain strings of the constant pool

What this does
  - `JSAotGenFunc.cpool_str` (new, after `cpool_numeric`): for every constant-pool entry, `cpool_str[i]` is the text of a
    JS_TAG_STRING entry that is 8-bit, has only characters 1..127 and is at most 15 bytes long, NUL terminated; every
    other entry (numbers, functions, wide or long strings, ropes, the empty string) reads "". The table is built with
    the numeric pool in the generator-info walk and freed with it in js_aot_gen_free.

Why we need it
  The generator folds `typeof x === "number"` (and the other typeof names) to a tag test; it has to know the string
  constant that the comparison names. The numeric pool carries only numbers. Earleyboyer's typeof tests are about
  1% of its instructions in the generic comparison.

Failure modes
  A failed allocation leaves `cpool_str` NULL; the consumer reads that as "no strings known" and keeps the generic op.
  No runtime path of the engine reads the table; it exists only in the -DQJS_AOT_GEN build.

Soundness
  A copy of immutable pool text taken while the function bytecode is alive; nothing in it aliases engine memory.
  Strings that are not plain short ASCII are never exported, so a consumer cannot mistake a wide or sliced string for
  its prefix.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -72825,0 +72826,25 @@
+                /* The short plain strings of the pool; a failed allocation leaves the table absent. */
+                if (b->cpool_count > 0 && b->cpool != NULL) {
+                    char (*strs)[16] = js_mallocz_rt(rt, 16 * (size_t)b->cpool_count);
+                    if (strs) {
+                        int ci;
+                        for (ci = 0; ci < b->cpool_count; ci++) {
+                            JSValue cv = b->cpool[ci];
+                            if (JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(cv) == JS_TAG_STRING) {
+                                JSString *sp = JS_VALUE_GET_STRING(cv);
+                                if (!sp->is_wide_char && sp->len <= 15) {
+                                    const uint8_t *sc = (const uint8_t *)strv(sp);
+                                    uint32_t k;
+                                    for (k = 0; k < sp->len; k++)
+                                        if (sc[k] == 0 || sc[k] > 127)
+                                            break;
+                                    if (k == sp->len) {
+                                        memcpy(strs[ci], sc, sp->len);
+                                        strs[ci][sp->len] = 0;
+                                    }
+                                }
+                            }
+                        }
+                        g->cpool_str = (const char (*)[16])strs;
+                    }
+                }
@@ -72898,0 +72924 @@
+            js_free_rt(rt, (void *)arr[i].cpool_str);
--- a/quickjs-aot-gen.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-gen.h
@@ -52,0 +53,4 @@
+    /* For every constant-pool entry, the text of a short plain string (8-bit characters 1..127, at most 15 bytes) and
+       "" for every other entry, so the generator can tell `typeof x === "number"` from any other comparison. Entry i
+       is `cpool_str[i]`, NUL terminated; an empty string and an entry that is not a short plain string both read "". */
+    const char (*cpool_str)[16];
